From 55970e8601569eb8d77c630f39a2562c35071998 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 22:30:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-658j-r8rw-q6mx (CVE-2026-115560):
 session.upload_progress.enabled off by default

The upload progress hook writes attacker-controlled data into the session
with the session's serializer. When an application reads the same session
with a different serializer, that can lead to code execution. Upstream
turned the feature off by default and added a runtime check of the
session INI settings.

In this tree the upload progress hook is already a no-op since the
CVE-2026-109618 fix (php_session_rfc1867_callback() returns early), so
this change only makes the default say so: session.upload_progress.enabled
now defaults to "0", also in the globals initialisation. The runtime
check is not backported, as in the upstream EOL backports.

Backport of php-src 3f70f66611 for EOL 7.2.34; the change is identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ext/session/session.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ext/session/session.c b/ext/session/session.c
index 40a38f8b..af215a02 100644
--- a/ext/session/session.c
+++ b/ext/session/session.c
@@ -816,7 +816,7 @@ PHP_INI_BEGIN()
 
 	/* Upload progress */
 	STD_PHP_INI_BOOLEAN("session.upload_progress.enabled",
-	                                                "1",     ZEND_INI_PERDIR, OnUpdateBool,        rfc1867_enabled, php_ps_globals, ps_globals)
+	                                                "0",     ZEND_INI_PERDIR, OnUpdateBool,        rfc1867_enabled, php_ps_globals, ps_globals)
 	STD_PHP_INI_BOOLEAN("session.upload_progress.cleanup",
 	                                                "1",     ZEND_INI_PERDIR, OnUpdateBool,        rfc1867_cleanup, php_ps_globals, ps_globals)
 	STD_PHP_INI_ENTRY("session.upload_progress.prefix",
@@ -2826,6 +2826,7 @@ static PHP_GINIT_FUNCTION(ps) /* {{{ */
 	ps_globals->mod = NULL;
 	ps_globals->serializer = NULL;
 	ps_globals->mod_data = NULL;
+	ps_globals->rfc1867_enabled = 0;
 	ps_globals->session_status = php_session_none;
 	ps_globals->default_mod = NULL;
 	ps_globals->mod_user_implemented = 0;
From cf12ff3936a06432dd30777da7348286dc090955 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:09:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-3qrf-m4j2-pcrr (CVE-2023-3823): reset libxml2 global
 defaults before parsing

libxml2 copies process-wide defaults (xmlSubstituteEntitiesDefault,
xmlLoadExtDtdDefaultValue, validation, ...) into every new parser context.
If anything in the process changed one of them, for example another
extension or library, PHP's XML parsers (dom, simplexml, xmlreader, xsl,
soap, xml) inherited it even though PHP never asked for it. Entity
substitution and external DTD loading turned on that way allow XXE.

The fix sets the defaults to known values around each parse
(PHP_LIBXML_SANITIZE_GLOBALS / PHP_LIBXML_RESTORE_GLOBALS) or sets the
options on the parser context directly.

Backport of php-src c283c3ab0b (Niels Dossche) with the zend_test helper
backport (zend_test_override_libxml_global_state, Remi Collet) that the
upstream tests use; zend_test is a test-only extension. Same change as
Sury's 7.2 patches 0111, 0112 and 0113 (7.2 adaptation of the zend_test part).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
