From 5c6d11ee09deb6036f1792ff36a5617249e63396 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:09:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix bug #81727 (CVE-2022-31629): cookie names mangled into
 __Host-/__Secure-

PHP turns "." and " " in variable names into "_", so a cookie named
"..Host-x" arrived as "__Host-x". A cookie set by a sibling subdomain or
over plain HTTP could then pose as a __Host-/__Secure- cookie, which
browsers only accept from the exact secure origin. Such names are now
discarded when the unmangled name did not have the prefix.

Backport of php-src 0611be4e82 (Derick Rethans), same change as Sury's 7.2
patch 0092. The NEWS hunk is left out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
