From 95b53debca09e3ef40767ff5d7996c2e6ada3e83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:09:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix bug #77423 (CVE-2020-7071): FILTER_VALIDATE_URL accepts
 invalid userinfo

FILTER_VALIDATE_URL accepted URLs whose user part holds characters that
RFC 3986 does not allow there. With such URLs the filter and the client
that later fetches the URL can disagree on the host, so validation could
not be trusted to keep requests to allowed hosts. The filter now rejects
a user part that is not valid userinfo.

Only the ext/filter part of php-src 4a89e726bd ("Alternative fix for bug
77423", Christoph M. Becker) is taken. Its other half (ext/standard/url.c
and the parse_url() tests that go with it) reverts the parse_url() change
of the first #77423 fix, which this tree has from Gentoo's
php-7.2.34-77423.patch and keeps, so parse_url() behaves as before.
Sury's 7.2 patch 0058 is the whole commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
