From c6c9067f40f4ed55762bba3621e154d149d70bf2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:09:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-453j-q27h-5p8x (CVE-2025-6491): SoapVar with a name
 over 2 GB

libxml2 before 2.13 leaves a node with a NULL name when xmlNodeSetName()
gets a name longer than 2 GB, and serialising the message then
dereferences it. The name is reset to a sentinel in that case. With
libxml2 2.13 and later the bug cannot happen; the change is harmless
there.

Backport of php-src 9cb3d8d200 (Ahmed Lekssays), same change as Sury's 7.2
patch 0187.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
